\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Cumulative returns of the directional trading strategies derived from individual base predictors (gray) compared to the naive, equally weighted ensemble average (orange) and the underlying buy-and-hold asset return (dashed black). This representative plot (evaluated on the QQQ dataset) highlights the extreme variance in individual model performance. By smoothing this variance, the ensemble average provides a stabilized comparative baseline for our subsequent CMAB evaluations.}}{13}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mean_cum_return}{{4}{13}{Cumulative returns of the directional trading strategies derived from individual base predictors (gray) compared to the naive, equally weighted ensemble average (orange) and the underlying buy-and-hold asset return (dashed black). This representative plot (evaluated on the QQQ dataset) highlights the extreme variance in individual model performance. By smoothing this variance, the ensemble average provides a stabilized comparative baseline for our subsequent CMAB evaluations}{figure.caption.5}{}}
